## Common Amazon SEO Problems We Fix

**Keyword-stuffed titles that kill CTR** Titles nobody will ever read will simply be skipped. Low Click Through rate(CTR) suggests the relevancy to A10 is poor, so that further damages your rank. Our titles have been optimized for algorithms AND for shoppers.

**Bullet points written as feature lists** Features show customers WHAT something is. Benefits show them WHY they care. We reformat and rewrite our bullets to focus first on the buyer's pain point, then support it with your product feature-a structure that converts.

**Wasted backend search term fields** The majority of people fill this space up with nothing or a bunch of redundant terms. We pack the full 250 bytes with long-tail Tier 3 keywords, synonyms, miss spellings and foreign equivalents.

**PPC masking organic decline** While your ad spend might be making your position look solid, your organic position is actually slowly falling behind. This is why you will see a drop like this if budget gets slashed… because of what your ranking has really been doing! From the get-go, we keep paid vs. Organic performance distinct, to help you know where you stand!

**One-time optimization mindset** The algorithm for Amazon is ever changing. Your competitors continue to update their products and seasonal keywords can fluctuate throughout the year. Amazon SEO is not something you can just “set and forget”-your competitors are taking notice and this can result in them stealing your traffic.

---

## Best Practices We Follow on Every Campaign

- Front-load seasonal keyword updates **6 to 8 weeks before peak demand periods**-not during them
- **Enroll in Brand Registry early**-A+ Content, Manage Your Experiments, and Brand Analytics all require it; every month without enrollment is lost conversion advantage
- **Optimize the first 80 characters of every title for mobile**-over 60% of Amazon traffic is mobile; that is what shoppers actually see
- **Drive external traffic deliberately**-social media, Google Shopping, and email campaigns pointing to priority ASINs send compound A10 ranking signals
- **Track organic and paid performance separately**-combined reporting hides the truth about where your revenue is actually coming from
- **Treat review management as an SEO function**-build review acquisition into every post-purchase touchpoint consistently, not reactively

